# ⚠ SHELL SCRIPTS MUST CHECK OUT WITH LF, ALWAYS.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows, where git's autocrlf normalises text files
# to CRLF in the working tree. That is harmless for JS and markdown and FATAL for
# a shell script: a `.sh` checked out with CRLF has a carriage return on the end
# of its shebang, so macOS answers
#
#     /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# ...and every line after it is wrong too. `desktop-agent/install.sh` and
# `neuro-desktop-agent.sh` are written here and RUN ON THE MAC, so they cross
# exactly that boundary. Same species as the byte-for-byte drift test that could
# never pass because one side was LF and the other CRLF — a difference invisible
# on the machine that created it.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The Pi runs these too.
*.bash text eol=lf
